0100 10100                              1 ; Configuration that can be used by the Arkos Tracker 3 players.
0100 10100                              3 ; It indicates what parts of code are useful to the song/sound effects, to save both memory and CPU.
0100 10100                              4 ; The players may or may not take advantage of these flags, it is up to them.
0100 10100                              6 ; You can either:
0100 10100                              7 ; - Ignore this file. The player will use its default build (no optimizations).
0100 10100                              8 ; - Include this to the source that also includes the player (BEFORE the player is included) (recommended solution).
0100 10100                              9 ; - Include or copy/paste this at the beginning of the player code (not recommended, the player should not be modified).
0100 10100                             11 ; This file was generated for a specific song. Do NOT use it for any other.
0100 10100                             12 ; Do NOT try to modify these flags, this can lead to a crash!
0100 10100                             14 ; If you use one player but several songs, don't worry, these declarations will stack up.
0100 10100                             15 ; Just make sure to include them, in any order, BEFORE the player.
