0690 10690                              1 ;       Arkos Tracker 3 player "generic" player.
0690 10690                              2 ;       By Targhan/Arkos.
0690 10690                              3 ;       Psg optimization trick on CPC by Madram/Overlanders.
0690 10690                              5 ;       v1.2:
0690 10690                              6 ;               - Added support for PCW and SVI. No change at all in the code, it uses the same access as MSX. Small label/constants refactor, but no Z80 change.
0690 10690                              7 ;               - Removed ":" before EQUs (to be compatible with RASM 2.3.9).
0690 10690                              8 ;               - Changed the MSX period table to 1789773 Hz (was 1773400 Hz like Spectrum before).
0690 10690                              9 ;               - Corrected a small conditional bug when the SFX has hardware sounds, but not the main song, using player configuration (thanks Arnaud!).
0690 10690                             10 ;       V1.1a: Added external variables instead of hardcoded constants inside the player:
0690 10690                             11 ;               - Declare PLY_AKG_REMOVE_HOOKS (PLY_AKG_REMOVE_HOOKS = 1) to remove hooks (previously was PLY_AKG_USE_HOOKS).
0690 10690                             12 ;               - Declare PLY_AKG_REMOVE_STOP_SOUNDS added to remove the snippet to stop the sounds (previously was PLY_AKG_STOP_SOUNDS) .
0690 10690                             13 ;               - Declare PLY_AKG_REMOVE_FULL_INIT_CODE added to remove full init code (see below) (previously was PLY_AKG_FULL_INIT_CODE).
0690 10690                             14 ;       V1.1
0690 10690                             15 ;               - Corrected a SoftwareAndHardware bug if using Player Configuration and forced hardware sound (without using forced software sound).
0690 10690                             16 ;               - Corrected a crash when using more than 128 effect blocks (thanks E-dredon and Roudoudou).
0690 10690                             17 ;
0690 10690                             18 ;       This compiles with RASM. Check the compatibility page on the Arkos Tracker website, it contains a source converter to any Z80 assembler!
0690 10690                             19 ;
0690 10690                             20 ;       The player uses the stack for optimizations. Make sure the interruptions are disabled before it is called.
0690 10690                             21 ;       The stack pointer is saved at the beginning and restored at the end.
0690 10690                             22 ;
0690 10690                             23 ;       Target hardware:
0690 10690                             24 ;       ---------------
0690 10690                             25 ;       This code can target Amstrad CPC, MSX, Spectrum, Pentagon, PCW and SVI (SpectraVideo). By default, it targets Amstrad CPC.
0690 10690                             26 ;       Simply use one of the follow line (BEFORE this player):
0690 10690                             27 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_CPC = 1
0690 10690                             28 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_MSX = 1
0690 10690                             29 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_SPECTRUM = 1
0690 10690                             30 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_PENTAGON = 1
0690 10690                             31 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_PCW = 1
0690 10690                             32 ;       PLY_AKG_HARDWARE_SVI = 1
0690 10690                             33 ;       Note that the PRESENCE of this variable is tested, NOT its value.
0690 10690                             34 ;
0690 10690                             35 ;       ROM
0690 10690                             36 ;       ----------------------
0690 10690                             37 ;       To use a ROM player (no automodification, use of a small buffer to put in RAM):
0690 10690                             38 ;       PLY_AKG_ROM = 1
0690 10690                             39 ;       PLY_AKG_ROM_Buffer = #4000 (or wherever).
0690 10690                             40 ;       This makes the player a bit slower and slightly bigger.
0690 10690                             41 ;       The buffer is PLY_AKG_ROM_BufferSize long (=250 bytes max, 273 with sound effects).
0690 10690                             42 ;       You can hardcode this value, because it is calculated, so it won't be accessible before this player is assembled.
0690 10690                             43 ;       This value decreases when you use player configuration, but increases if you use sound effects.
0690 10690                             44 ;
0690 10690                             45 ;       Optimizations:
0690 10690                             46 ;       --------------
0690 10690                             47 ;       - Use the Player Configuration of Arkos Tracker 3 to generate a configuration file to be included at the beginning of this player.
0690 10690                             48 ;         It will disable useless features according to your songs, saving for memory and CPU! Check the manual for more details, or more simply the testers.
0690 10690                             49 ;       - SIZE: Hooks for external calls (play/init) are present by default. Define PLY_AKG_REMOVE_HOOKS to remove them (PLY_AKG_REMOVE_HOOKS = 1).
0690 10690                             50 ;       - SIZE: Define PLY_AKG_REMOVE_STOP_SOUNDS to remove the Stop sound method (PLY_AKG_Stop) if you don't intend on stopping the music.
0690 10690                             51 ;       - SIZE: If you play your song "one shot" (i.e. without looping it), you can define PLY_AKG_REMOVE_FULL_INIT_CODE, some
0690 10690                             52 ;         initialization code will not be assembled.
0690 10690                             54 ;       Sound effects:
0690 10690                             55 ;       --------------
0690 10690                             56 ;       Sound effects are disabled by default. Declare PLY_AKG_MANAGE_SOUND_EFFECTS to enable it:
0690 10690                             57 ;       PLY_AKG_MANAGE_SOUND_EFFECTS = 1
0690 10690                             58 ;       Check the sound effect tester to see how it enables it.
0690 10690                             59 ;       Note that the PRESENCE of this variable is tested, NOT its value.
0690 10690                             61 ;       Additional note:
0690 10690                             62 ;       - There can be a slightly difference when using volume in/out effects compared to the PC side, because the volume management is
0690 10690                             63 ;         different. This means there can be a difference of 1 at certain frames. As it shouldn't be a bother, I let it this way.
0690 10690                             64 ;         This allows the Z80 code to be faster and simpler.
0690 10690                             65 ;
0690 10690                             66 ;       -------------------------------------------------------
