0CC6 10CC6                           2421 ;Codes that read InstrumentCells.
0CC6 10CC6                           2422 ;IN:    HL = pointer on the Instrument data cell to read.
0CC6 10CC6                           2423 ;       IX = can be modified.
0CC6 10CC6                           2424 ;       IYL = Instrument step (>=0). Useful for retrig.
0CC6 10CC6                           2425 ;       SP = normal use of the stack, do not pervert it!
0CC6 10CC6                           2426 ;       D = register 7, as if it was the channel 3 (so, bit 2 and 5 filled only).
0CC6 10CC6                           2427 ;             By default, the noise is OFF, the sound is ON, so no need to do anything if these values match.
0CC6 10CC6                           2428 ;       E = inverted volume.
0CC6 10CC6                           2429 ;       A = SET BELOW: first byte of the data, shifted of 3 bits to the right.
0CC6 10CC6                           2430 ;       B = SET BELOW: first byte of the data, unmodified.
0CC6 10CC6                           2431 ;       HL' = track pitch.
0CC6 10CC6                           2432 ;       DE' = 0 / note (instrument + Track transposition).
0CC6 10CC6                           2433 ;       BC' = temp, use at will.
0CC6 10CC6                           2435 ;OUT:   HL = new pointer on the Instrument (may be on the empty sound). If not relevant, any value can be returned, it doesn't matter.
0CC6 10CC6                           2436 ;       IYL = Not 0 if retrig for this channel.
0CC6 10CC6                           2437 ;       D = register 7, updated, as if it was the channel 1 (so, bit 2 and 5 filled only).
0CC6 10CC6                           2438 ;       E = volume to encode (0-16).
0CC6 10CC6                           2439 ;       HL' = software period. If not relevant, do not set it.
0CC6 10CC6                           2440 ;       DE' = output period.
